  "## About me\n\nWelcome to my creative journey. My work is a testament to my commitment to bringing ideas to life, where each pixel becomes a brushstroke in the canvas of imagination.\n\nI find inspiration in the world around me, whether through the pages of a captivating novel, the intricate details of typography, or the vibrant hues of nature during my outdoor escapades.\n\nIf you're curious to dive deeper into my work, you can follow me:": "",
  "## Data We Collect\n\nWhen you contact us or engage our services, we collect:\n\n- **Contact information**: name, email, phone, company\n- **Service inquiry details** and project information\n- **Communication records** related to service delivery\n- **Business information** necessary for consulting and business setup\n\n## How We Use Your Data\n\n- To provide requested services and communicate about projects\n- To send service updates, reports, and relevant information\n- To improve our services and website experience\n- To coordinate with authorities in business setup processes (with your consent)\n\n## Data Sharing\n\nWe do not sell your data. We may share information with:\n\n- **Service providers** necessary for project delivery (with your consent)\n- **Licensed professionals** (brokers, banks, legal advisors, designers) when coordinating regulated services\n- **UAE authorities** when required for business setup processes\n- **Authorities** when required by law\n\n## Your Rights (GDPR Compliance)\n\nIf you are in the EU, you have the right to:\n\n- Access your personal data\n- Request correction or deletion\n- Withdraw consent for processing\n- Request data portability\n\nContact us at **info@bestvisual.ae** to exercise these rights.\n\n## Data Security\n\nWe use industry-standard security measures to protect your information. Data is stored securely and accessed only by authorized personnel.\n\n## Cookies\n\nThis website uses essential cookies for functionality and analytics cookies to understand site usage. You can control cookie preferences through your browser settings.\n\n## Contact for Privacy Matters\n\nFor privacy questions or requests: **info@bestvisual.ae**\n\n_Last Updated: June 2026_": "",
  "## Scope of Services\n\nBest Visual FZE provides coordination, advisory, strategic consulting, content creation, design, and operational support services as described on this website. We do not provide regulated legal advice, tax advice, or regulated financial services unless explicitly coordinated through licensed professionals.\n\n## Client Responsibilities\n\nClients are responsible for verifying that services meet their specific regulatory, legal, and business requirements in their jurisdiction. Where services involve coordination with third parties (banks, brokers, authorities), the client relationship with those parties is governed by their respective terms.\n\n## Intellectual Property\n\nFor design and content creation services: intellectual property rights to final deliverables transfer to the client upon completion of payment. Best Visual retains the right to display work in its portfolio unless otherwise agreed in writing.\n\n## Limitation of Liability\n\nBest Visual coordinates services in good faith but does not guarantee outcomes that depend on third-party decisions (loan approvals, regulatory timelines, market conditions, government approvals). Our liability is limited to the fees paid for services rendered.\n\n## Jurisdiction\n\nThese terms are governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates. Disputes are subject to the jurisdiction of Ras Al Khaimah courts.\n\n_Last Updated: June 2026_": "",
  "## Why a Free Zone?\n\nUAE Free Zones offer 100% foreign ownership, zero corporate tax (for qualifying activities), full repatriation of profits, and no currency restrictions. For international service businesses, consultancies, and trading companies, a Free Zone is often the most efficient structure.\n\nThe trade license itself can be issued in **3 to 7 working days** once your documentation is complete. But full operational readiness — including visa processing and corporate bank account opening — realistically takes **4 to 8 weeks**.\n\n## The 6-Week Timeline\n\n### Week 1: Define Your Setup\n\n- Choose your Free Zone (RAKEZ, DMCC, IFZA, Meydan, etc.)\n- Select your legal structure (FZE, FZC, or branch)\n- Define your business activities (typically 1–10 related activities per license)\n- Confirm office requirements (flexi-desk, shared, or physical office)\n\n### Week 2: Document Preparation\n\n- Passport copies (shareholders, managers)\n- Visa or entry stamp copy\n- Passport-sized photographs\n- Business plan (required by some Free Zones)\n- Specimen signature forms\n- No-objection certificate if currently employed in UAE\n\n### Week 3: Application & Payment\n\n- Submit application to the Free Zone authority\n- Pay license and registration fees\n- Receive initial approval (typically 2–5 working days)\n\n### Week 4: License Issuance\n\n- Trade license issued\n- Establishment card issued\n- Lease agreement finalized (flexi-desk or office)\n- Share certificates issued\n\n### Weeks 5–6: Visa & Banking\n\n- Entry permit application\n- Medical fitness test\n- Emirates ID application\n- Visa stamping in passport\n- Corporate bank account application (can take 2–4 weeks independently)\n\n## What Most Timelines Miss\n\nThe trade license is fast. The bottleneck is almost always the **corporate bank account**. UAE banks have strict compliance requirements, and account opening can take 2–6 weeks depending on the bank, your nationality, and your business activity.\n\n**Practical tip**: Start the bank account process as soon as your trade license is issued. Do not wait until visas are complete.\n\n## Checklist Summary\n\n- [ ] Free Zone selected\n- [ ] Business activities defined\n- [ ] Legal structure chosen\n- [ ] Passport copies prepared\n- [ ] Application submitted\n- [ ] Fees paid\n- [ ] Trade license received\n- [ ] Establishment card received\n- [ ] Visa process initiated\n- [ ] Bank account application submitted\n- [ ] Emirates ID received\n- [ ] Visa stamped\n\n## Do You Need Help?\n\nBusiness setup involves coordination across multiple authorities, banks, and service providers. If you want someone to manage the process end-to-end — from Free Zone selection through to visa stamping and bank account opening — [get in touch with us](/contact).": "",
